course: dictionary
lesson: 13830
title: IV: a number, a drip and a king
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: IV is a Roman numeral. The Romans used letters to make numbers: I is 1, V is 5 and X is 10. When a smaller letter comes before a bigger one, you take the small one away. IV is 5 take away 1, so IV means 4. «Chapter IV starts on page 40» means chapter four starts on page 40.
explain: IV is also short for «intravenous», which means into a vein. «The nurse put an IV in his arm so he could get fluid.» An IV is a thin tube, also called a drip, that gives fluid or medicine straight into a vein. Doctors and nurses often use short forms like this.
explain: You will also see IV after the names of kings, queens and popes. «Henry IV» means Henry the Fourth. Look at the words around IV to tell which meaning it has: a number in a chapter, a drip in a hospital, or a name in history.
fact: IV is a Roman numeral that means 4.
fact: I before V means 5 take away 1, so IV is 4.
fact: An IV is a drip that gives fluid or medicine into a vein.
fact: IV is short for «intravenous», which means into a vein.
fact: «Henry IV» means Henry the Fourth, a king's name.
exercise: «Turn to chapter IV on page 12.» What number is IV? | *Four | Five | Three
exercise: «The nurse set up an IV for the patient.» What is an IV? | A kind of cake | A small bed | A bandage | *A drip that gives fluid or medicine into a vein
exercise: Which is the Roman numeral for 4? | V | X | *IV | I
test: «Henry IV was a king of England.» What does IV mean here? | *The Fourth | A medicine | Ivy, a green plant | Five
test: The nurse said, «Keep the IV in until the fluid runs out.» What is the IV? | The number 5 | *A drip into a vein | A type of fish | A short cut
exam: In «Chapter IV», what number is IV? | *Four | One | Six | Five
